1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,690
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,690 --> 00:00:05,150
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:06,280
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:08,060
I've worked on a garbage

5
00:00:08,060 --> 00:00:09,820
truck for twenty-eight
years.

6
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:11,590
Jumping on and off that
truck

7
00:00:11,590 --> 00:00:13,450
hundreds of times a shift.

8
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:14,630
I had my right knee

9
00:00:14,630 --> 00:00:16,150
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:16,430 --> 00:00:18,270
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:18,410 --> 00:00:19,670
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:19,710 --> 00:00:20,890
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:20,890 --> 00:00:22,000
and it went away.

14
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:23,320
This is different.

15
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:23,940
Tight.

16
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:24,710
Full.

17
00:00:25,010 --> 00:00:25,830
Like a band around

18
00:00:25,830 --> 00:00:27,510
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:27,550 --> 00:00:28,650
And for two years I've

20
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:30,010
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:30,050 --> 00:00:31,260
Give it time.

22
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:33,380
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:34,720
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,170
At three months,

25
00:00:36,170 --> 00:00:37,270
give it six.

26
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:38,230
At six months,

27
00:00:38,230 --> 00:00:39,960
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:41,120
At a year,

29
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:42,880
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:42,990 --> 00:00:44,170
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:45,350
We went down the list.

32
00:00:45,390 --> 00:00:46,800
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:46,990 --> 00:00:47,950
Every session,

34
00:00:47,950 --> 00:00:49,600
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:49,890 --> 00:00:51,070
I got stronger.

36
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:52,770
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:52,970 --> 00:00:54,390
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:54,390 --> 00:00:55,610
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:55,830 --> 00:00:57,790
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:57,790 --> 00:00:58,870
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:58,870 --> 00:01:00,100
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:01,430
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:01,490 --> 00:01:03,440
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:05,130
And after that, a second

45
00:01:05,130 --> 00:01:06,340
operation to go back

46
00:01:06,340 --> 00:01:07,650
in and do it over.

47
00:01:07,690 --> 00:01:08,800
I said no.

48
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:11,160
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

49
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:12,200
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:13,880
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:16,360
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:18,060
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:19,550
for it and went to work.

54
00:01:19,670 --> 00:01:21,110
Couldn't do the stairs,

55
00:01:21,110 --> 00:01:22,270
couldn't stand at the
counter

56
00:01:22,270 --> 00:01:23,930
long enough to finish
dinner,

57
00:01:23,930 --> 00:01:25,430
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

58
00:01:25,430 --> 00:01:28,090
game without shifting
every two minutes.

59
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:29,230
On the route,

60
00:01:29,230 --> 00:01:30,400
every jump off the back

61
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:31,510
of that truck went
straight

62
00:01:31,510 --> 00:01:32,440
to my knee,

63
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:33,330
and I'd climb back

64
00:01:33,330 --> 00:01:34,540
on and do it again.

65
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:36,100
It woke me at night,

66
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:38,310
and it turned ordinary
things,

67
00:01:38,310 --> 00:01:39,800
like climbing up into the
truck

68
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,170
or up off the couch,

69
00:01:41,170 --> 00:01:42,320
into a decision.

70
00:01:42,630 --> 00:01:43,820
After a long and serious

71
00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:44,970
talk with my wife,

72
00:01:44,970 --> 00:01:47,150
I went back in one more
time.

73
00:01:47,510 --> 00:01:48,630
That was the fourth set

74
00:01:48,630 --> 00:01:50,120
of X-rays on this knee.

75
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:51,790
And like the three before
it,

76
00:01:51,790 --> 00:01:54,020
the answer was everything
looks great.

77
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:56,160
No loosening, no
infection,

78
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:57,110
nothing wrong.

79
00:01:57,290 --> 00:01:58,680
Only this time

80
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:00,130
there was no new number.

81
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:01,430
Nobody said

82
00:02:01,430 --> 00:02:02,810
give it another six
months.

83
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:04,750
There was nothing left to
give it.

84
00:02:05,030 --> 00:02:06,080
I sat in the parking

85
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,010
lot for a while.

86
00:02:07,050 --> 00:02:08,050
Okay, I thought.

87
00:02:08,090 --> 00:02:09,340
Then explain this.

88
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:11,720
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

89
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:13,170
I hit my breaking point.

90
00:02:13,490 --> 00:02:15,530
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

91
00:02:15,730 --> 00:02:17,590
Everyone in the house was
asleep

92
00:02:17,590 --> 00:02:19,300
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

93
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:20,380
with my leg up,

94
00:02:20,380 --> 00:02:21,850
trying to find any angle

95
00:02:21,850 --> 00:02:22,700
where it didn't feel like

96
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:24,540
something was wrapped
around my knee

97
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:25,420
and tightening.

98
00:02:25,870 --> 00:02:26,980
I had a route to start

99
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:28,200
in a few hours.

100
00:02:28,290 --> 00:02:31,050
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

101
00:02:31,210 --> 00:02:33,050
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

102
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:34,340
And I just thought,

103
00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:36,010
is this really my life
now?

104
00:02:36,050 --> 00:02:37,530
I can't live like this.

105
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:39,710
So I made myself a
promise.

106
00:02:39,810 --> 00:02:40,830
I wouldn't go a day

107
00:02:40,830 --> 00:02:42,430
without looking for an
answer.

108
00:02:42,670 --> 00:02:44,020
And when I found one,

109
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:45,080
I'd share it with everyone

110
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:46,480
going through the same
thing.

111
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:48,170
So I got my laptop out

112
00:02:48,170 --> 00:02:49,040
and went looking.

113
00:02:49,090 --> 00:02:50,320
Not for a product.

114
00:02:50,470 --> 00:02:51,880
For an explanation.

115
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:54,040
Mayo Clinic forums,

116
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:56,310
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

117
00:02:56,310 --> 00:02:58,640
doctor videos, medical
animations.

118
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:00,300
And that's when I found a
video

119
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:01,850
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

120
00:03:01,890 --> 00:03:04,270
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

121
00:03:04,270 --> 00:03:05,980
had been through exactly
this.

122
00:03:06,210 --> 00:03:07,990
But before I say anything
else,

123
00:03:07,990 --> 00:03:09,380
I want to be straight with
you.

124
00:03:09,820 --> 00:03:11,750
You've already had
something work fast.

125
00:03:11,790 --> 00:03:12,660
The ice.

126
00:03:12,770 --> 00:03:14,300
The first week of a new
pill.

127
00:03:14,340 --> 00:03:15,770
The good day after a
session.

128
00:03:15,810 --> 00:03:17,010
Then it wore off.

129
00:03:17,050 --> 00:03:19,130
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

130
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:21,350
Fast relief isn't relief.

131
00:03:21,470 --> 00:03:22,400
It's a preview.

132
00:03:22,670 --> 00:03:23,600
So I'm not going to tell

133
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:24,870
you this works fast.

134
00:03:24,910 --> 00:03:25,720
It doesn't.

135
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:27,660
But if you're willing to
be patient,

136
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:28,440
and to look at what's

137
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:30,240
going on around your new
knee

138
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:31,730
instead of inside it,

139
00:03:31,730 --> 00:03:33,210
there is a real reason

140
00:03:33,210 --> 00:03:34,390
it still hurts.

141
00:03:34,510 --> 00:03:36,480
And something you can do
about it.

142
00:03:36,770 --> 00:03:38,100
Let me explain what he
said,

143
00:03:38,100 --> 00:03:39,520
because this is what
changed

144
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:40,630
everything for me.

145
00:03:40,910 --> 00:03:42,740
He started with the
basics.

146
00:03:42,860 --> 00:03:44,260
A knee replacement takes
out

147
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:46,020
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

148
00:03:46,020 --> 00:03:47,400
in metal and plastic.

149
00:03:47,590 --> 00:03:49,400
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

150
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:50,890
you had before the
operation.

151
00:03:51,340 --> 00:03:52,610
That part I already knew.

152
00:03:52,910 --> 00:03:54,250
But then he explained
something

153
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:55,630
nobody had ever told me.

154
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:56,200
He said,

155
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:57,450
think about a swollen foot

156
00:03:57,450 --> 00:03:58,540
inside a shoe.

157
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:00,020
The shoe didn't shrink.

158
00:04:00,190 --> 00:04:02,130
Your foot is taking up
more room,

159
00:04:02,130 --> 00:04:03,550
so everything feels
cramped

160
00:04:03,550 --> 00:04:04,860
and tight and squeezed.

161
00:04:05,010 --> 00:04:06,280
Your new knee sits

162
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:08,110
in a limited space with
living

163
00:04:08,110 --> 00:04:09,730
tissue packed all around
it.

164
00:04:09,870 --> 00:04:11,620
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

165
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:13,180
had to work through that
tissue.

166
00:04:13,430 --> 00:04:16,330
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

167
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:17,970
At first that's normal.

168
00:04:18,190 --> 00:04:19,500
But in some people

169
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,030
that swelling can stay
switched

170
00:04:21,030 --> 00:04:22,950
on far longer than
expected.

171
00:04:23,110 --> 00:04:25,550
And swollen tissue takes
up more room

172
00:04:25,550 --> 00:04:27,070
than calm tissue does.

173
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:29,190
So when you bend,

174
00:04:29,190 --> 00:04:30,860
that tissue gets
compressed.

175
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:32,100
When you straighten,

176
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:33,200
it gets pulled tight.

177
00:04:33,490 --> 00:04:34,530
That's the band.

178
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:35,760
That's the ache

179
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:37,160
that never quite leaves.

180
00:04:37,270 --> 00:04:38,300
And you start being

181
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:39,570
the one who says,

182
00:04:39,570 --> 00:04:40,570
you go ahead.

183
00:04:40,650 --> 00:04:41,700
I'll stay here.

184
00:04:41,870 --> 00:04:43,430
And that's exactly why so
much

185
00:04:43,430 --> 00:04:45,630
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

186
00:04:45,940 --> 00:04:47,940
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

187
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:48,940
around the knee.

188
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:49,920
Worth doing,

189
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:50,800
and I'd done it.

190
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:52,570
It does nothing about
tissue

191
00:04:52,570 --> 00:04:53,630
taking up room.

192
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:54,960
A nerve block quiets

193
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:56,620
the nerve carrying the
signal.

194
00:04:56,900 --> 00:04:59,340
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

195
00:04:59,570 --> 00:05:01,530
But when that irritated
tissue

196
00:05:01,530 --> 00:05:03,250
finally calms down,

197
00:05:03,250 --> 00:05:04,670
it holds less fluid,

198
00:05:04,670 --> 00:05:06,270
and it takes up less room.

199
00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:08,130
Less room taken up

200
00:05:08,130 --> 00:05:10,450
means less pressure
squeezing the joint.

201
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:12,540
That's what takes the
pressure off.

202
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:14,250
After two years of this,

203
00:05:14,250 --> 00:05:15,840
it finally made sense.

204
00:05:16,170 --> 00:05:18,090
The problem was never the
new knee.

205
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:20,130
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

206
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:21,980
He calls it the squeeze.

207
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:24,500
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

208
00:05:24,780 --> 00:05:26,250
I'd bought knee sleeves,

209
00:05:26,250 --> 00:05:28,530
compression braces,
creams,

210
00:05:28,530 --> 00:05:30,330
half of Amazon really,

211
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:31,600
and all any of it gave

212
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:32,680
me was an hour.

213
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:34,030
I even looked at going

214
00:05:34,030 --> 00:05:35,930
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

215
00:05:36,010 --> 00:05:38,050
But at $200 a session

216
00:05:38,050 --> 00:05:39,840
with nothing covered by
insurance,

217
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,130
that was a quick no.

218
00:05:41,170 --> 00:05:42,280
Then one night I went

219
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:43,550
back to that knee
replacement

220
00:05:43,550 --> 00:05:45,010
group and actually read
it.

221
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:46,600
Thousands of people,

222
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:48,220
years out from surgery,

223
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:50,510
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

224
00:05:50,510 --> 00:05:51,860
nobody could explain.

225
00:05:52,230 --> 00:05:53,960
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

226
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:55,710
the same thing kept coming
up.

227
00:05:55,750 --> 00:05:57,740
This one device,

228
00:05:57,740 --> 00:05:59,240
and people saying it was
the first

229
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:00,630
thing that made a
difference.

230
00:06:00,930 --> 00:06:03,100
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

231
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:04,430
alright, here it comes,

232
00:06:04,430 --> 00:06:05,770
he's selling me something,

233
00:06:05,770 --> 00:06:07,410
let me shut that down
right now.

234
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,080
I'm only here because I
made myself

235
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:11,070
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

236
00:06:11,070 --> 00:06:12,020
that if I ever found

237
00:06:12,020 --> 00:06:13,140
something that helped,

238
00:06:13,140 --> 00:06:14,160
I'd say so.

239
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:16,510
It's called the KenRelief
Red

240
00:06:16,510 --> 00:06:17,850
Light Therapy Wrap.

241
00:06:18,130 --> 00:06:19,950
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

242
00:06:20,210 --> 00:06:21,320
It looked like the cheap

243
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:23,100
knee sleeves off Amazon

244
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:24,580
that did nothing for me.

245
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:26,790
But I went to their
website anyway,

246
00:06:26,790 --> 00:06:27,690
just to see what all

247
00:06:27,690 --> 00:06:28,730
the fuss was about.

248
00:06:29,090 --> 00:06:31,100
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

249
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:33,700
charge $200 a session for,

250
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:36,740
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

251
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:37,720
in a wrap you plug

252
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:39,000
into the wall at home.

253
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:40,950
Two hundred and forty
lights.

254
00:06:41,090 --> 00:06:43,010
Red at 660 nanometers

255
00:06:43,010 --> 00:06:45,360
and near-infrared at 850,

256
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:47,620
run together for the
strongest effect.

257
00:06:47,890 --> 00:06:49,360
Four strength levels.

258
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:51,260
A five to thirty minute
timer.

259
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:53,390
Then I saw the guarantee.

260
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:55,240
Ninety days.

261
00:06:55,310 --> 00:06:57,780
Results or your money
back,

262
00:06:57,780 --> 00:07:00,380
no questions, no store
credit,

263
00:07:00,380 --> 00:07:02,180
and you don't even send it
back.

264
00:07:02,530 --> 00:07:04,920
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

265
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:06,480
days to change my mind.

266
00:07:06,570 --> 00:07:07,880
There wasn't much to lose,

267
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:08,850
so I ordered it.

268
00:07:09,350 --> 00:07:10,830
Two of them, actually.

269
00:07:11,010 --> 00:07:12,930
Only the right knee was
replaced,

270
00:07:12,930 --> 00:07:15,150
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

271
00:07:15,150 --> 00:07:16,840
and I'd done it for two
years.

272
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:19,150
The left one was carrying
the difference.

273
00:07:19,260 --> 00:07:20,190
When it came,

274
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:22,380
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

275
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:23,490
because I'd been let down

276
00:07:23,490 --> 00:07:25,380
too many times to get
excited.

277
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:27,070
What I felt was warmth.

278
00:07:27,250 --> 00:07:29,240
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

279
00:07:29,470 --> 00:07:30,660
More like it was coming

280
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:32,240
from inside the knee

281
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:33,680
and spreading around it.

282
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:34,870
And that was it.

283
00:07:35,070 --> 00:07:36,730
That was the whole
experience.

284
00:07:36,770 --> 00:07:37,790
When I took it off,

285
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:38,430
I'll be honest,

286
00:07:38,430 --> 00:07:40,160
nothing dramatic had
happened.

287
00:07:40,380 --> 00:07:41,950
And after what that video
said,

288
00:07:41,950 --> 00:07:43,830
that's exactly what I
expected.

289
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:44,910
What was different

290
00:07:44,910 --> 00:07:46,130
was that for the first

291
00:07:46,130 --> 00:07:47,560
time in two years

292
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:49,500
I'd done something for my
knee

293
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:50,540
